From e1801782bb1e4b16d7076d991d4f6fff0f6a1e4d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PanVK WSI Debug <debug@localhost>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 09:27:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] panvk/csf: bridge imported sync files through stock kbase
 queues

Queue native fence waits through the existing KCPU FENCE_WAIT and CQS_SET_OPERATION ABI, then wait on the event in each dependent GPU subqueue. No kernel changes are required.
Keep wait-only submits and exported sync files pending until their external dependencies complete. Separate wait and signal KCPU queues per Vulkan queue to avoid cross-queue head-of-line blocking.
Probe support before queuing a real wait, retain the CPU path when unsupported, and fail closed after a partial enqueue. Keep event memory alive until GPU groups and KCPU commands are terminated.
---
